
# The post: the data the blog draws and stores. On its own, so a view that draws posts imports the record and not the
# store beside it: ./post holds the repository over the database and re-exports this, and a program that only draws
# (the blog in a terminal, with a store that keeps nothing) carries no database runtime (terminal-target-0005).

form post
  link id, like text
  link title, like text
  link body, like text
